.github.com/users/JeffreySanford","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JeffreySanford/public-sector-federation/commits/aec4f7debbf099b52ae5a3d79830fef4c799f5c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T16:31:43Z","email":"jeffreysanford@gmail.com","name":"Jeffrey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T16:31:43Z","email":"jeffreysanford@gmail.com","name":"Jeffrey"},"message":"Add manifest-generated component status table to Starlight (Phase 2)\n\nAdd ComponentStatusTable.astro, which imports\npackages/ui-patterns/generated/component-manifest.json directly at\nAstro build time and renders a live table of all 21 manifest entries\n(lifecycle, provider, Storybook, tests, manual a11y review, Figma) on\nthe Starlight components page. This is the first concrete step of doc\n10''s Phase 2 \"system-health and evidence data into generated views\"\nitem: unlike the existing hand-authored flagship prose and the\nhand-maintained documentation-integrity.json, this table is read\ndirectly from the manifest and cannot drift from it.\n\nConvert components/index.md to .mdx to support the component import.\nUpdate doc 10 with an honest assessment of the other two Phase 2\nitems: the ~50 engineering docs under docs/design-system/ have not\nbeen moved into Starlight (and whether they should be is an open scope\ndecision, since Starlight is already a deliberately curated site\nrather than a mirror), and historical-process archiving has not\nstarted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db798119b90a3a9608b426e13ac459123e552933","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JeffreySanford/public-sector-federation/git/trees/db798119b90a3a9608b426e13ac459123e552933"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JeffreySanford/public-sector-federation/git/commits/aec4f7debbf099b52ae5a3d79830fef4c799f5c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":