point for the paraphrase page-finder\n(baseline ~45-50%). Findings, all measured on pf2e with a noise-controlled paired\nmethod (same cached queries per arm, so the delta is trustworthy at n=80):\n\n- ef_search: default 40 slightly under-recalls vs an exact scan (0.30 -> 0.33 in\n  the diagnostic). 200 reaches the exact-scan ceiling at negligible latency, no\n  keyword-arm regression (hybrid recall@10 0.93). This is the change shipped.\n- HyDE (embed an LLM hypothetical): REGRESSES -12/80 (4 wins, 16 losses),\n  recall@10 0.45 -> 0.30. On this adventure-heavy corpus the hypothetical\n  hallucinates generic content that lands farther from the real obscure page.\n  Not shipped.\n- Entity-assist (fuse entity-semantic hits mapped to page_number): page recall@10\n  0.46 -> 0.42; entity chunks don''t match page-theme paraphrases. Not shipped.\n\nConclusion: ~45-50% is the embedding-model ceiling (MiniLM-L6, short-query vs\nshort-summary) — exact recall@10 is ~0.33-0.50, so no search-time lever gets near\n80% on deliberately keyword-free paraphrases against a single target among ~19k.\nReaching the setpoint needs a stronger embedding model (= re-embed the whole\ncorpus), tracked as separate work. Live queries carry keyword overlap where\nhybrid already wins (keyword recall@10 0.93), so real page-finding beats the\nadversarial number.","tree":{"sha":"bd7101475a0aa0138a9d6272006872df922f516b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/bd7101475a0aa0138a9d6272006872df922f516b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/42922b17d164f6c6dd32ecefe6fe3a5154677565","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/42922b17d164f6c6dd32ecefe6fe3a5154677565","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKDQyOTIyYjE3ZDE2NGY2YzZkZDMyZWNlZmU2ZmUzYTUxNTQ2Nzc1NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/f20a00fcb928fb1b0cd9fe63f5b98408ecd03a84","sha":"f20a00fcb928fb1b0cd9fe63f5b98408ecd03a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/f20a00fcb928fb1b0cd9fe63f5b98408ecd03a84"}],"sha":"42922b17d164f6c6dd32ecefe6fe3a5154677565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/42922b17d164f6c6dd32ecefe6fe3a5154677565"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/f20a00fcb928fb1b0cd9fe63f5b98408ecd03a84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T10:40:17Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T18:14:05Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"feat(search): semantic + hybrid summary search for the fallback page-finder\n\nSummaries had a search path, but it was FTS-only — the embedding column, the\nper-space HNSW cosine index on source_summaries, and the embed tasks all existed\nfor semantic summary search, but no query ever read them. So the \"find the right\npage\" fallback was blind to paraphrase: a query worded unlike the summary text\nreturned nothing.\n\n- Add semantic_summary_search: per-table ANN arms (each with its own ORDER BY\n  embedding <=> vec + LIMIT so it uses that table''s cosine index; exact scan on\n  the tiny extraction tables). Filters mirror fts_summary_search exactly — the\n  legacy source_summaries table is always queried and filtered by its level\n  COLUMN, while page/chapter/book tables are included/excluded by identity — so\n  both legs fuse the same candidate universe.\n- Add hybrid_summary_search: RRF (K=60) of the lexical + semantic legs, fused on\n  row id. Deliberately separate from entity hybrid_search — summaries stay a\n  drill-down tool (find the page, then `search` its content), not folded into\n  the primary entity ranking.\n- Wire both the REST endpoint (routers/search.py) and the MCP search_summaries\n  tool to the hybrid path (embed the query, then fuse).\n\nNo migration: source_summaries is already HNSW-indexed per partition; page/\nchapter/book are 1-130 rows where an exact scan is faster and exact until they\ngrow past a few thousand.\n\nEval (evals/eval_summary_retrieval.py, 40 pf2e page summaries, paraphrase +\nkeyword arms — the keyword arm guards against regressing lexical lookups):\n  paraphrase  fts MRR 0.000 (recall@10 0.00!) -> hybrid 0.329 (recall@10 0.50)\n  keyword     fts MRR 0.856 -> hybrid 0.942  (no regression; hybrid improves it)\n  +~1ms median latency. Deterministic unit tests cover ANN order, RRF fusion,\n  the FTS-blind-but-semantic-finds case, and the level=''page'' legacy-row filter.","tree":{"sha":"c70fb8c66a0fe88aa960ade9ac7b23c8b8062570","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/c70fb8c66a0fe88aa960ade9ac7b23c8b8062570"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/f20a00fcb928fb1b0cd9fe63f5b98408ecd03a84","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/f20a00fcb928fb1b0cd9fe63f5b98408ecd03a84","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKGYyMGEwMGZjYjkyOGZiMWIwY2Q5ZmU2M2Y1Yjk4NDA4ZWNkMDNhODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/5dc494ef2098535e98f46d2233e2b20c10fbce55","sha":"5dc494ef2098535e98f46d2233e2b20c10fbce55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/5dc494ef2098535e98f46d2233e2b20c10fbce55"}],"sha":"f20a00fcb928fb1b0cd9fe63f5b98408ecd03a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/f20a00fcb928fb1b0cd9fe63f5b98408ecd03a84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/5dc494ef2098535e98f46d2233e2b20c10fbce55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T00:26:15Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T18:14:01Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"feat(worker): reconciliation sweep for dropped embedding dispatches\n\nThe extraction→embedding cross-dispatch is best-effort: a broker outage during\ningest is caught and logged, the ingest still succeeds, and the affected rows\nkeep embedding = NULL forever with nothing to retry them (Mode 2 of the seam —\nthe failure the name/queue contract test doesn''t cover). Content silently stays\nunsearchable.\n\nAdd a periodic reconciliation sweep as the backstop:\n\n- gm_compendium.reembed_missing (embedding worker): embeds any row that has\n  carried embedding = NULL longer than a 30-min staleness window, across all\n  four embed-bearing tables, reusing the existing per-id embed helpers. Inline,\n  idempotent, monotonic — embedded rows stop matching, so runs converge; the\n  staleness window skips healthy in-flight embeds so a hit is a real dropped-\n  dispatch signal and is logged WARNING. Bounded 500/table/run.\n- Run by embedded beat (`-B` in Dockerfile.worker) every 30 min. Setpoint:\n  ~4k rows/hr recovery; a dropped row self-heals within ~30–60 min.\n- Guard the new silent-failure surfaces in the contract test: the sweep task is\n  registered, beat_schedule references it by constant (a typo''d schedule fires\n  nothing), its queue matches, and Dockerfile.worker keeps `-B` (dropping it\n  silently stops the sweep) — all mutation-checked.\n\nVerified end-to-end against the dev DB: one run embedded exactly 500 stale\nsource_summaries (19598→19098), entities/page/chapter no-op. NB: that 19k\nbacklog is a real pre-existing gap the trickle sweep alone drains slowly — a\none-off bulk backfill is the faster path if wanted.","tree":{"sha":"b7da508cb7bbf121ca50e60b1d225927c2817d41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/b7da508cb7bbf121ca50e60b1d225927c2817d41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/5dc494ef2098535e98f46d2233e2b20c10fbce55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/5dc494ef2098535e98f46d2233e2b20c10fbce55","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKDVkYzQ5NGVmMjA5ODUzNWU5OGY0NmQyMjMzZTJiMjBjMTBmYmNlNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/a997f85280011aac1a1c24d2c59ecfc9027b4565","sha":"a997f85280011aac1a1c24d2c59ecfc9027b4565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/a997f85280011aac1a1c24d2c59ecfc9027b4565"}],"sha":"5dc494ef2098535e98f46d2233e2b20c10fbce55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/5dc494ef2098535e98f46d2233e2b20c10fbce55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/a997f85280011aac1a1c24d2c59ecfc9027b4565/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T23:47:25Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T18:13:57Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"refactor(celery): centralize cross-app task/queue names + add a contract test\n\nThe extraction worker dispatches embedding work to the embedding worker by a\nbare task-name string on a shared queue, with the API doing the same for both\ntask families. Nothing linked the sender strings to the consuming apps at\nimport or test time, so a rename or queue change published to a task/queue\nnobody consumes: send_task raises nothing, the job reports success, and the\naffected rows keep embedding = NULL. Coupling-by-convention with no guard.\n\n- Add gm_compendium_core/celery_contract.py as the single source of truth for\n  every cross-app task name and the two queue names; import it at all send and\n  consume sites (worker/extraction decorators, extraction cross-dispatch, all\n  API router dispatches) so a rename lands in exactly one place.\n- Pin the embedding worker''s task_default_queue to EMBED_QUEUE so the consumed\n  queue is a config fact (it launches with no -Q), and standardize the API\n  embed sends to pass queue=EMBED_QUEUE explicitly (was relying on the default).\n- Add tests/test_celery_contract.py (pure, no DB): asserts every contract name\n  is registered on the consuming app, the registries match the contract exactly\n  both ways, the default queues line up, no dispatch site uses a literal name,\n  the sender-file list is complete (a dispatch in an unlisted file fails the\n  test), and Dockerfile.worker grows no -Q that diverges from EMBED_QUEUE.\n  Mutation-checked: name drift, config-queue drift, launch-flag (-Q) drift, and\n  a new unguarded dispatch site each turn it red.\n\nBehavior is unchanged — the constant values equal the prior literals and the\npinned queue equals the prior default. 365 passed (the 13 chat failures are the\npre-existing Python 3.14 breakage, unrelated).","tree":{"sha":"a020cb4972e588a70170924b385c893dd661bbf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/a020cb4972e588a70170924b385c893dd661bbf0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/a997f85280011aac1a1c24d2c59ecfc9027b4565","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/a997f85280011aac1a1c24d2c59ecfc9027b4565","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKGE5OTdmODUyODAwMTFhYWMxYTFjMjRkMmM1OWVjZmM5MDI3YjQ1NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/66e013dfb27ff8f57ff5be8c22c5302407068cb1","sha":"66e013dfb27ff8f57ff5be8c22c5302407068cb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/66e013dfb27ff8f57ff5be8c22c5302407068cb1"}],"sha":"a997f85280011aac1a1c24d2c59ecfc9027b4565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/a997f85280011aac1a1c24d2c59ecfc9027b4565"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/66e013dfb27ff8f57ff5be8c22c5302407068cb1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T23:29:17Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T18:13:53Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"feat(nginx): persist structured JSON access/error logs to a bind-mounted dir\n\nnginx logged only the default combined format to stdout, captured solely by\ncontainerd''s log driver — no retained history and gone on container recreate.\n\nAdd a json_access log_format (escape=json so scanner junk can''t break the\nJSON) and write access.log + error.log to /var/log/nginx-json, bind-mounted\nfrom infra/nginx/logs/ so usage history survives recreation. Keep the combined\nstdout sink so `nerdctl logs` is unchanged. Ship infra/nginx/logrotate.conf\n(USR1 reopen) for rotation, and sync the canonical nginx run block in CLAUDE.md\nto include the certs/certbot/logs mounts the real container already uses.","tree":{"sha":"393cff9ac94d2898ad6727291b99b6c7a53d105a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/393cff9ac94d2898ad6727291b99b6c7a53d105a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/66e013dfb27ff8f57ff5be8c22c5302407068cb1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/66e013dfb27ff8f57ff5be8c22c5302407068cb1","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKDY2ZTAxM2RmYjI3ZmY4ZjU3ZmY1YmU4YzIyYzUzMDI0MDcwNjhjYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/476b0974a5b564924568a4800f28d078e5b9b8d5","sha":"476b0974a5b564924568a4800f28d078e5b9b8d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/476b0974a5b564924568a4800f28d078e5b9b8d5"}],"sha":"66e013dfb27ff8f57ff5be8c22c5302407068cb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/66e013dfb27ff8f57ff5be8c22c5302407068cb1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/476b0974a5b564924568a4800f28d078e5b9b8d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T14:11:55Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:03:15Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"fix(db): migration 0020 — allow the `editor` role in users_role_chk\n\n0019 pinned users.role to CHECK IN (''user'',''admin''), so seeding the new editor\naccount (feat: gate source PDFs behind admin+editor) trips the constraint and\ncrashes the API on startup — including on a fresh public-repo deploy. 0020\nwidens the CHECK to (''user'',''admin'',''editor''), idempotent via DROP IF EXISTS.","tree":{"sha":"e2833db6fb61ac58ff70664eba0bd8958730c86f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/e2833db6fb61ac58ff70664eba0bd8958730c86f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/476b0974a5b564924568a4800f28d078e5b9b8d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/476b0974a5b564924568a4800f28d078e5b9b8d5","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKDQ3NmIwOTc0YTViNTY0OTI0NTY4YTQ4MDBmMjhkMDc4ZTViOWI4ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/7e26c78712ea32c942106754ebc6d5e6f6464b0d","sha":"7e26c78712ea32c942106754ebc6d5e6f6464b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/7e26c78712ea32c942106754ebc6d5e6f6464b0d"}],"sha":"476b0974a5b564924568a4800f28d078e5b9b8d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/476b0974a5b564924568a4800f28d078e5b9b8d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/7e26c78712ea32c942106754ebc6d5e6f6464b0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:57:38Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:03:14Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"feat(auth): gate source PDFs/Verify view behind admin + new editor role\n\nLets the app be shared for feedback without exposing watermarked source PDFs.\nAdds an `editor` role (normal-user powers + source-file access, no admin\nrights) and a `require_pdf_access` dependency (role ∈ {admin, editor}) on the\nfour PDF-serving endpoints: full file/download, page-as-PDF, page.png (Verify\nview), and page-images. Extracted text, search, and chat stay open to any\nauthenticated user — only the raw watermarked files lock down.\n\n- auth.py: `require_pdf_access`; config.py: editor_username/password; main.py:\n  seed the editor account (blank password skips, like the others); compose:\n  EDITOR_USERNAME/EDITOR_PASSWORD env.\n- Backend enforces via cookie or bearer (native <img>/<iframe> PDF requests\n  carry only the cookie). Router→decorator→param dep order makes a `user`\n  token a deterministic 403 before space lookup.\n- Frontend `canViewPdf()` hides the PDF/Verify view modes (PageViewPage), the\n  PDF download link (SourceDetailPage), and the PDF badge/filter (SourcesPage)\n  for everyone else; the backend 403s direct hits regardless.\n- 18 new access-control tests (unit rule + all four endpoints × user-403 /\n  editor-passes / anon-401). Full suite: 156 api + 90 frontend green.","tree":{"sha":"8400d71259df4f7d15e48296ce03d220e939bf62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/8400d71259df4f7d15e48296ce03d220e939bf62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/7e26c78712ea32c942106754ebc6d5e6f6464b0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/7e26c78712ea32c942106754ebc6d5e6f6464b0d","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKDdlMjZjNzg3MTJlYTMyYzk0MjEwNjc1NGViYzZkNWU2ZjY0NjRiMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/5082ea67f8286814a8acdab789d7691da8ec7b8f","sha":"5082ea67f8286814a8acdab789d7691da8ec7b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/5082ea67f8286814a8acdab789d7691da8ec7b8f"}],"sha":"7e26c78712ea32c942106754ebc6d5e6f6464b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/7e26c78712ea32c942106754ebc6d5e6f6464b0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/5082ea67f8286814a8acdab789d7691da8ec7b8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:58:25Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:03:13Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"feat(search): case-insensitive prefix source-scoping in list_entities & list_summaries\n\nExtends the search engine''s `_build_source_filter` behaviour to the two list\nendpoints so all three agree on book scoping: a friendly source name (\"Season of\nGhosts\") now matches every volume of a series (\"Season of Ghosts 1 of 4 — …\")\ninstead of requiring an exact source string.\n\n- list_entities: `sources @> ARRAY[source]` exact-match → `EXISTS (unnest(sources)\n  … ILIKE :prefix)`, with the prefix LIKE-escaped.\n- list_summaries: `source == x` → `source ILIKE x%` (escaped).\n\nDrops the now-unused cast/ARRAY/Text imports the exact-match path needed. 25\nlist/source/summary tests green.","tree":{"sha":"4a2f3ab95646cf9f233571bcda061b726400bb13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/4a2f3ab95646cf9f233571bcda061b726400bb13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/5082ea67f8286814a8acdab789d7691da8ec7b8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/5082ea67f8286814a8acdab789d7691da8ec7b8f","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKDUwODJlYTY3ZjgyODY4MTRhOGFjZGFiNzg5ZDc2OTFkYThlYzdiOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/409908cdb9d4ebe20abe20c1f3088904b21b70da","sha":"409908cdb9d4ebe20abe20c1f3088904b21b70da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/409908cdb9d4ebe20abe20c1f3088904b21b70da"}],"sha":"5082ea67f8286814a8acdab789d7691da8ec7b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/5082ea67f8286814a8acdab789d7691da8ec7b8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/409908cdb9d4ebe20abe20c1f3088904b21b70da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:49:47Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:03:12Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"feat(extraction): normalize entity_type at ingest to stop misleading/duplicate types\n\nThe vision LLM free-assigns entity_type, which drifts into inconsistent or\nnear-duplicate types — pf2e''s core skills landed as `rule` (they''re skills; the\nactual rules are `game_mechanic`), a mislabel that dead-ended type-filtered\nretrieval. New `entity_types.normalize_entity_type(raw, aliases)` is a single\nchoke point: mechanical hygiene (casefold + collapse whitespace/hyphens to\nunderscores; falsy -> \"other\") then a per-space alias map from\n`metadata.extraction.type_aliases`.\n\nWired at both ingest choke points — the pf2e vision path (ingest.py Step 6, both\nthe LLM-extract and combined-OCR branches) and the structured-corpus path\n(corpus_ingest.py: pages, concepts, distilled summaries). pf2e preset ships\n`extraction.type_aliases = {\"rule\": \"skill\"}`, reflecting that the LLM only ever\nused `rule` for skills in this corpus; reversible via config. Absent config it''s\nmechanical-only, so other corpora and REST/MCP are unaffected.\n\nThis is the recurrence guard for the live retype (17 skills rule->skill): a\nre-ingest of Player Core now produces `skill`, not `rule`. 10 new unit tests;\nfull extraction suite (119) green.","tree":{"sha":"a852558cabe2ab55cd12c5e0e4aadca1a8bb0a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/a852558cabe2ab55cd12c5e0e4aadca1a8bb0a6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/409908cdb9d4ebe20abe20c1f3088904b21b70da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/409908cdb9d4ebe20abe20c1f3088904b21b70da","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKDQwOTkwOGNkYjlkNGViZTIwYWJlMjBjMWYzMDg4OTA0YjIxYjcwZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/dc6c322719e25e1906cfb6fff300ead754020c76","sha":"dc6c322719e25e1906cfb6fff300ead754020c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/dc6c322719e25e1906cfb6fff300ead754020c76"}],"sha":"409908cdb9d4ebe20abe20c1f3088904b21b70da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/409908cdb9d4ebe20abe20c1f3088904b21b70da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/dc6c322719e25e1906cfb6fff300ead754020c76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:45:39Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:03:11Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"fix(search): soft type-preference in the chat adapter (replaces empty-only fallback)\n\nThe prior commit''s \"retry unfiltered when a type filter returns zero rows\"\nguard never fired for the real failure: a wrong `types` guess usually returns\nnon-empty WRONG-type rows, not empty. E.g. types=\"rule\" for an aquatic-combat\nquestion returned the 6 core skills (Acrobatics, Athletics, ...) — non-empty,\nso no fallback — while the actual rules (typed game_mechanic) were excluded.\nThe golden 0->partial I attributed to that fallback was orchestrator variance.\n\nReplace it with a genuine soft filter in _chat_search: search UNFILTERED, then\nstable-float entities whose type matches the orchestrator''s requested `types`\nto the top. Requested types are preferred; off-type entities remain as graceful\nfallback, so a wrong/too-narrow/nonexistent type guess degrades instead of\ndead-ending. This makes the taxonomy''s granularity non-load-bearing for answer\nquality — the routing fragility, not the labels, was the real problem.\n\nREST/MCP callers keep hard `types` filtering (an explicit user choice); only the\nagent adapter softens it. Verified: golden \"aquatic combat\" 0/5 -> 5/5 runs\nstating all three facts; full golden 94.5% with 0 forbidden-claim violations\n(absent queries still decline — soft filter returns nearest neighbours, same as\nbefore, so the model declines on relevance not emptiness).\n\nPaired with a live-data correction (the 17 pf2e core skills retyped rule->skill;\nfts/embeddings unaffected — both derive from name/content, not entity_type) and\nan extraction-time type-normalization guard (separate commit) to stop the\nfree-assigning vision LLM re-minting misleading types on future ingests.","tree":{"sha":"a42138efabd12b3f991517ebda7da78700d5fb73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/a42138efabd12b3f991517ebda7da78700d5fb73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/dc6c322719e25e1906cfb6fff300ead754020c76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/dc6c322719e25e1906cfb6fff300ead754020c76","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKGRjNmMzMjI3MTllMjVlMTkwNmNmYjZmZmYzMDBlYWQ3NTQwMjBjNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/b332123aa51f94c54c97d7ee6ebeec79f82fe53b","sha":"b332123aa51f94c54c97d7ee6ebeec79f82fe53b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/b332123aa51f94c54c97d7ee6ebeec79f82fe53b"}],"sha":"dc6c322719e25e1906cfb6fff300ead754020c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/dc6c322719e25e1906cfb6fff300ead754020c76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/b332123aa51f94c54c97d7ee6ebeec79f82fe53b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:20:42Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:03:09Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"fix(search): recover from type-filter dead-ends + punctuation-proof name matching\n\nDigging into the one golden-eval miss (\"rules for fighting underwater\") traced\nto two search bugs, one operative and one latent:\n\n1. Type-filter dead-end (the operative cause). The orchestrator searched\n   types=\"rule\", but pf2e stores those rules as game_mechanic entities, so the\n   hard AND-filter returned zero rows on every attempt — a dead end with no\n   signal to broaden, and the narrator answered from unrelated Swim content.\n   _chat_search now retries once unfiltered when a type-restricted search finds\n   nothing (agent-path only; REST/MCP defaults unchanged), tagging the response\n   with type_filter_relaxed. The named rule then surfaces via hybrid''s\n   name-mention leg. Golden aquatic: 0/3 -> 1/3 runs stating all three facts.\n\n2. Punctuation-glued n-grams (latent, hits UI users typing verbatim).\n   _norm_match stripped only hyphens/apostrophes, so a query\n   \"...(aquatic combat)?\" tokenized to \"(aquatic\", \"combat)?\" and the\n   name-mention n-gram never equaled the entity name \"Aquatic Combat\". Now it\n   maps all punctuation to spaces, symmetrically on query and name, so\n   exact-match semantics hold.\n\nAlso adds eval_golden --only <substring> to run a single question cheaply.\n\nResidual (documented, not fixed here): the corpus has near-duplicate rule\nentities — a crunchy game_mechanic and a prose guidance/`Rules` version — and\nthe game_mechanic:-0.12 type penalty ranks the crunchy one below the prose one\nfor queries that don''t name the rule. That''s a data-quality/tuning matter\n(source-aware boosts or entity dedup), not to be fixed by blindly detuning the\npenalty. 17 search unit tests green.","tree":{"sha":"9ca209176ea48d273e6b99c95f00c9dbe64139f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/9ca209176ea48d273e6b99c95f00c9dbe64139f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/b332123aa51f94c54c97d7ee6ebeec79f82fe53b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/b332123aa51f94c54c97d7ee6ebeec79f82fe53b","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKGIzMzIxMjNhYTUxZjk0YzU0Yzk3ZDdlZTZlYmVlYzc5ZjgyZmU1M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/80cb953a91a5aee0ba3d2d217d3175b83446c230","sha":"80cb953a91a5aee0ba3d2d217d3175b83446c230","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/80cb953a91a5aee0ba3d2d217d3175b83446c230"}],"sha":"b332123aa51f94c54c97d7ee6ebeec79f82fe53b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/b332123aa51f94c54c97d7ee6ebeec79f82fe53b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/80cb953a91a5aee0ba3d2d217d3175b83446c230/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T11:30:21Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:03:05Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"fix(evals): repair the three stale evals against the current stack\n\nRunning the suite to baseline surfaced that half of it had drifted:\n\n- eval_agent: ToolContext gained a required `corpus_get_page` arg; every\n  turn threw instantly (0 answers/0 tool calls). Pass it, matching eval_golden.\n- eval_agentic: posted to nginx :8080, which now 301-redirects HTTP→HTTPS\n  (empty body), and sent no auth to the now-gated API. Hit the API directly\n  on :8000 and send the API_KEY as a Bearer token (read from infra/.env).\n- eval_summaries: called `.complete()` on the chat client, which only\n  streams — swapped to the extraction OpenAILLMClient (the real ingest\n  summary interface), and raised max_tokens 600→1500 so a reasoning model''s\n  hidden tokens don''t truncate the JSON summary (15/20 parse errors → 1/20).\n\nAll six evals now green. Baseline: golden 97.2% fact-recall; retrieval\nsemantic/hybrid 0.75 recall@10; agentic 100% on every behavior metric;\nsummaries faithfulness 3.79 / coverage 4.26; narrator med 7-11s.","tree":{"sha":"b6a96dd11f05b17f3d03a52eaacb3ce1ac95364a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/b6a96dd11f05b17f3d03a52eaacb3ce1ac95364a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/80cb953a91a5aee0ba3d2d217d3175b83446c230","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/80cb953a91a5aee0ba3d2d217d3175b83446c230","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKDgwY2I5NTNhOTFhNWFlZTBiYTNkMmQyMTdkMzE3NWI4MzQ0NmMyMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/c6a0dd44f81812ab32b054afb5716dc685cf3c0c","sha":"c6a0dd44f81812ab32b054afb5716dc685cf3c0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/c6a0dd44f81812ab32b054afb5716dc685cf3c0c"}],"sha":"80cb953a91a5aee0ba3d2d217d3175b83446c230","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/80cb953a91a5aee0ba3d2d217d3175b83446c230"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/commits/c6a0dd44f81812ab32b054afb5716dc685cf3c0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T02:43:53Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:03:04Z","email":"nick.cammorato@gmail.com","name":"Nick Cammorato"},"message":"test(evals): commit the chat/retrieval quality harness as evals/\n\nPromote the reusable eval scripts out of the local scripts/ pile into a proper\nevals/ harness (they were dropped in the repo-hygiene \"infra only\" cut, but\nthey''re reusable quality tooling, not one-off ops):\n\n- eval_golden (answer quality vs a fixed golden set of checkable factual claims),\n  eval_agent (e2e agent), eval_agentic (orchestrator behavior), eval_retrieval\n  (FTS vs semantic vs hybrid), eval_narrator_latency (model A/B latency+cost),\n  eval_summaries (summary quality).\n- evals/README.md documents prerequisites (live stack + OPENROUTER_API_KEY, run\n  from repo root), what each measures, and the golden-set overlap.\n- No secrets or copyrighted prose ship (golden set = uncopyrightable factual\n  claims; key from env/infra/.env; local-dev DSN only). Outputs (eval_results.json)\n  stay gitignored.\n\nNot pytest units — they drive the running app + an LLM, so they''re a manual/gated\nharness, distinct from tests/.","tree":{"sha":"8422b3941037cb1c96ffa80a0ed30831d003744f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/trees/8422b3941037cb1c96ffa80a0ed30831d003744f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cammoraton/compendium/git/commits/c6a0dd44f81812ab32b054afb5716dc685cf3c0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton","id":1749347,"login":"cammoraton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDkzNDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cammoraton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/c6a0dd44f81812ab32b054afb5716dc685cf3c0c","node_id":"C_kwDOTTydStoAKGM2YTBkZDQ0ZjgxODEyYWIzMmIwNTRhZmI1NzE2ZGM2ODVjZjNjMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cammoraton/compendium/commit/136a5ef750322e5e79d9d2515ff3ebb3b17019c6","sha":"136a5ef750322e5e79d9d2515ff3ebb3b17019c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos