ollowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan","id":3496697,"login":"tosdan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY2OTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commit/823773a03f5f1b633f424626ffa5feee1d58bd10","node_id":"C_kwDOTUX0U9oAKDgyMzc3M2EwM2Y1ZjFiNjMzZjQyNDYyNmZmYTVmZWVlMWQ1OGJkMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commit/f6e83d0281065d8e11eab74ba402c42f8913ac89","sha":"f6e83d0281065d8e11eab74ba402c42f8913ac89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/f6e83d0281065d8e11eab74ba402c42f8913ac89"}],"sha":"823773a03f5f1b633f424626ffa5feee1d58bd10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/823773a03f5f1b633f424626ffa5feee1d58bd10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3496697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan","id":3496697,"login":"tosdan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY2OTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/f6e83d0281065d8e11eab74ba402c42f8913ac89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T07:00:04Z","email":"3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"tosdan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T07:00:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: cover capturing real traffic and replaying it as prepared mocks (T5) (#11)\n\n* test: cover capturing real traffic and replaying it as prepared mocks (T5)\n\nAdd mockxy-capture, a standalone instance with the admin API. The fake\nbackend gains recognizable (status 202, body, x-receipt-id header) and\nbinary responses under /capture/. Its per-path arrival counter now\ncovers /identity/ and /capture/ through GET /api/arrivals.\n\ncapture-replay.spec.js generates backend responses from the browser,\nfinds them with a filtered Monitor cursor and reads the full entry by\nid and runtimeId. It then calls create-mocks with explicit choices,\nchecking per-item outcomes even on 201. The new endpoint stays disabled\nand the browser keeps reaching the backend until it is explicitly\nenabled; from then on the mock serves the captured status, body and\nheader without calling the backend. add-variant on an existing endpoint\nprepares an identifiable, inactive variant, and behavior changes only\nwhen it is selected. A binary capture becomes an incomplete, disabled\ndraft flagged INCOMPLETE_CAPTURE. A lost create-mocks response fails\nwithout a retry.\n\nThe setup helper gains readMonitorEntry, createMocksFromMonitor (single\nrequest, CREATE_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN on a lost response) and requireWritten.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: link PR #11 in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: lose the create-mocks response deterministically (T5 review)\n\nThe lost-response test used a 1 ms client timeout, which can expire\nbefore the request is sent: a helper retrying twice, with both attempts\naborted, still passed. A local test proxy now forwards every request to\nmockxy-capture. For create-mocks it waits for the engine''s full response\n(the creation happened) and then drops the client connection. The test\nchecks:\n- exactly one create-mocks request;\n- the lost 201 with the created item;\n- one endpoint with one variant in the catalog.\n\nA helper that retries fails with two requests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2bf2ae3c7f773dbd1af8e83a2418a221b8c9c1de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/trees/2bf2ae3c7f773dbd1af8e83a2418a221b8c9c1de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/commits/f6e83d0281065d8e11eab74ba402c42f8913ac89","verification":{"payload":"tree 2bf2ae3c7f773dbd1af8e83a2418a221b8c9c1de\nparent cbaec537f3ab3276ea7678a283dde45635675152\nauthor tosdan <3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790838004 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790838004 +0200\n\ntest: cover capturing real traffic and replaying it as prepared mocks (T5) (#11)\n\n* test: cover capturing real traffic and replaying it as prepared mocks (T5)\n\nAdd mockxy-capture, a standalone instance with the admin API. The fake\nbackend gains recognizable (status 202, body, x-receipt-id header) and\nbinary responses under /capture/. Its per-path arrival counter now\ncovers /identity/ and /capture/ through GET /api/arrivals.\n\ncapture-replay.spec.js generates backend responses from the browser,\nfinds them with a filtered Monitor cursor and reads the full entry by\nid and runtimeId. It then calls create-mocks with explicit choices,\nchecking per-item outcomes even on 201. The new endpoint stays disabled\nand the browser keeps reaching the backend until it is explicitly\nenabled; from then on the mock serves the captured status, body and\nheader without calling the backend. add-variant on an existing endpoint\nprepares an identifiable, inactive variant, and behavior changes only\nwhen it is selected. A binary capture becomes an incomplete, disabled\ndraft flagged INCOMPLETE_CAPTURE. A lost create-mocks response fails\nwithout a retry.\n\nThe setup helper gains readMonitorEntry, createMocksFromMonitor (single\nrequest, CREATE_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN on a lost response) and requireWritten.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: link PR #11 in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: lose the create-mocks response deterministically (T5 review)\n\nThe lost-response test used a 1 ms client timeout, which can expire\nbefore the request is sent: a helper retrying twice, with both attempts\naborted, still passed. A local test proxy now forwards every request to\nmockxy-capture. For create-mocks it waits for the engine''s full response\n(the creation happened) and then drops the client connection. The test\nchecks:\n- exactly one create-mocks request;\n- the lost 201 with the created item;\n- one endpoint with one variant in the catalog.\n\nA helper that retries fails with two requests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvgT0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf4sQAF89+Gfy1GEw4F9y9KasKg4m\nNU3b5QrbL+dBJIjXsQTEl+j9kVCu49Alodi1QO0XUnydHy9isIM+IGuhDu2gRVg6\naBCAwhc69hCzK6yXpeidKp6l0wI7LyX9VJ1xUA2wd/aUyBS65b/8MHBbH8mk1wOa\nThDKcqnAkElrZgo7SA1wg