nature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3496697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan","id":3496697,"login":"tosdan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY2OTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commit/cbaec537f3ab3276ea7678a283dde45635675152","node_id":"C_kwDOTUX0U9oAKGNiYWVjNTM3ZjNhYjMyNzZlYTc2NzhhMjgzZGRlNDU2MzU2NzUxNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commit/8935f698794e28aadac9773f6fbff28771e23b24","sha":"8935f698794e28aadac9773f6fbff28771e23b24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/8935f698794e28aadac9773f6fbff28771e23b24"}],"sha":"cbaec537f3ab3276ea7678a283dde45635675152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/cbaec537f3ab3276ea7678a283dde45635675152"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3496697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan","id":3496697,"login":"tosdan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY2OTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/8935f698794e28aadac9773f6fbff28771e23b24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T00:37:55Z","email":"3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"tosdan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T00:37:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: cover ephemeral runtime configuration and existing connections (T4) (#10)\n\n* test: cover ephemeral runtime configuration and existing connections (T4)\n\nAdd mockxy-config, a standalone instance with the admin API, and a second\nfake backend (backend-b). The fake backend now reports its identity and\ncounts arrivals per path under /identity/, and /ws/identity names the\nbackend in its greeting and echoes. The existing routes are unchanged.\n\nruntime-config.spec.js checks from the browser that an override changes\nGET /config, the config revision and the next request (CORS on, off,\nexplicit, removed). backendUrl null disables the backend while unset\nrestores the startup one. A request already inside the engine stays on\nthe old backend while it is still in the delay: the barrier is the\ncontainer''s \"Request received.\" log line, and the backend counter\nconfirms it had not arrived when the switch was applied. The next\nrequest uses the new backend, and an open WebSocket tunnel stays on its\noriginal backend.\n\nruntime-config-restart.spec.js restarts the instance in a new\nchromium-config-restart project, chained after chromium-stack-mutating:\na new runtimeId, no overrides, and runtime_changed on the old Monitor\ncursor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: link PR #10 in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: restore startup configuration around the restart test (T4 review)\n\nThe restart test applied three overrides with no cleanup, so a failure\nbefore or during the restart left backend B, CORS off and a global delay\non the instance. withStartupRestored now removes every override before\nthe action and again afterwards, even when the action fails, waiting a\nbounded time for the instance to answer since it may be mid-restart.\n\nA regression test reproduces the review case: overrides applied, then a\nsimulated docker compose restart failure. The instance must end with no\noverrides; without the finally the test fails. Both tests in the file run\nin order in one worker.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: give the restart cleanup its own time budget (T4 review)\n\nThe startup restore ran in a finally that shared the 30 s test timeout,\nwhile it may wait up to 60 s for an instance that is mid-restart: a test\ntiming out with the instance unreachable left the overrides in place.\nThe restore now lives in beforeEach/afterEach hooks (tests/config-restore.js)\nthat extend their own timeout with testInfo.setTimeout.\n\nTwo regression tests run an inner spec in a child Playwright process and\ncheck the instance afterwards: an immediate error after the overrides,\nand a test that times out while the container is paused for 20 s, longer\nthan the child''s 8 s timeout, which is also a hook''s normal budget.\nWithout the budget extension the second fails with the overrides still\nactive. A guard fails the check if the pause did not actually last.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: isolate the child runner output and measure the actual pause (T4 review)\n\nThe child Playwright run shared test-results with the main suite and\nemptied it on start. It now writes into a temporary run directory\ncreated and removed by the outer test; a sentinel artifact of the main\nsuite must survive the child run.\n\nThe guard measured the whole child run, including its startup, so a\nshort pause could pass after a slow start. The inner test now runs\ndocker compose pause synchronously and records when it succeeded. The\ndetached resumer records the resume only if docker compose unpause\nsucceeds, which fails when the container is no longer paused. The\nouter test requires both markers and an actual pause of at least 20 s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7840565fb36cf21cca94e5e08b140ddb356cc05f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/trees/7840565fb36cf21cca94e5e08b140ddb356cc05f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/commits/8935f698794e28aadac9773f6fbff28771e23b24","verification":{"payload":"tree 7840565fb36cf21cca94e5e08b140ddb356cc05f\nparent c1bcb907cec85541849c770b88b3fd9f7254a3a9\nauthor tosdan <3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790815075 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790815075 +0200\n\ntest: cover ephemeral runtime configuration and existing connections (T4) (#10)\n\n* test: cover ephemeral runtime configuration and existing connections (T4)\n\nAdd mockxy-config, a standalone instance with the admin API, and a second\nfake backend (backend-b). The fake backend now reports its identity and\ncounts arrivals per path under /identity/, and /ws/identity names the\nbackend in its greeting and echoes. The existing routes are unchanged.\n\nruntime-config.spec.js checks from the browser that an override changes\nGET /config, the config revision and the next request (CORS on, off,\nexplicit, removed). backendUrl null disables the backend while unset\nrestores the startup one. A request already inside the engine stays on\nthe old backend while it is still in the delay: the barrier is the\ncontainer''s \"Request received.\" log line, and the backend counter\nconfirms it had not arrived when the switch was applied. The next\nrequest uses the new backend, and an open WebSocket tunnel stays on its\noriginal backend.\n\nruntime-config-restart.spec.js restarts the instance in a new\nchromium-config-restart project, chained after chromium-stack-mutating:\na new runtimeId, no overrides, and runtime_changed on the old Monitor\ncursor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: link PR #10 in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: restore startup configuration around the restart test (T4 review)\n\nThe restart test applied three overrides with no cleanup, so a failure\nbefore or during the restart left backend B, CORS off and a global delay\non the instance. withStartupRestored now removes every override before\nthe action and again afterwards, even when the action fails, waiting a\nbounded time for the instance to answer since it may be mid-restart.\n\nA regression test reproduces the review case: overrides applied, then a\nsimulated docker compose restart failure. The instance must end with no\noverrides; without the finally the test fails. Both tests in the file run\nin order in one worker.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: give the restart cleanup its own time budget (T4 review)\n\nThe startup restore ran in a finally that shared the 30 s test timeout,\nwhile it may wait up to 60 s for an instance that is mid-restart: a test\ntiming out with the instance unreachable left the overrides in place.\nThe restore now lives in beforeEach/afterEach hooks (tests/config-restore.js)\nthat extend their own timeout with testInfo.setTimeout.\n\nTwo regression tests run an inner spec in a child Playwright process and\ncheck the instance afterwards: an immediate error after the overrides,\nand a test that times out while the container is paused for 20 s, longer\nthan the child''s 8 s timeout, which is also a hook''s normal budget.\nWithout the budget extension the second fails with the overrides still\nactive. A guard fails the check if the pause did not actually last.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: isolate the child runner output and measure the actual pause (T4 review)\n\nThe child Playwright run shared test-results with the main suite and\nemptied it on start. It now writes into a temporary run directory\ncreated and removed by the outer test; a sentinel artifact of the main\nsuite must survive the child run.\n\nThe guard measured the whole child run, including its startup, so a\nshort pause could pass after a slow start. The inner test now runs\ndocker compose pause synchronously and records when it succeeded. The\ndetached resumer records the resume only if docker compose unpause\nsucceeds, which fails when the container is no longer paused. The\nouter test requires both markers and an actual pause of at least 20 s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvatjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPuYQAKXn/89RolpbQVEvp4L2CZhu\n0ca8e6N16Eg6pyICad1oOyHPS2rJWE0JBAp/mnfEx1C/tFR8Z7NxvBPwESuFfrUr\nG7D4u+S1O83sqICpIdGYzIzyOtbhZItRv7KJVNPdJhXfT0rDVQ4O6Xw6pnA/G1zT\nxe/VQOspTowujPW0RdKaivb3lDcy6bvEhqmnjPJ2bRgCkK1+5rxL8tGc9fCLFZI1\n+DBb8ADLMZVhwtZOW1N3Zn+CC+RSzQcgZQbYdkMSCeEeuA2jMX7L82+H6lZqYx+1\ncGN2bdcPEIPUhPXjEt+FP3u607sKoPsyp8qJEUgLvVAvMw3GZ/dckyTnY4viI4qJ\nAYH0zOlxrebELNYpRos8YwIF13JXwWblzGjMCHR2KrUY4fanuWw9qMvWZAjtYaK4\nx5i2lG+I7GVqFuqmm5SwnBuuzso/43VC1ZPctLMSdt910Txqzv47HYjiXcO+pEa1\ndROr/sVYY1zLZkgd