pi.github.com/users/tosdan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/dd8a6dbfc8ac943bfd9722ceda48f88ce8f1dbbe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T23:22:31Z","email":"3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"tosdan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T23:22:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: cover the repeatable agent setup through API, browser and Monitor (T3) (#9)\n\n* test: cover the repeatable agent setup through API, browser and Monitor (T3)\n\nAdd mockxy-setup, a standalone instance with the admin API whose CORS\nstarts disabled, and an external setup helper (tests/agent-setup.js). It\nchecks the served contract and the workspace, declares CORS and delays\nthrough PATCH /config, prepares contents with the revision it read, then\nactivates and resets, failing with a diagnostic code instead of\nretrying.\n\nagent-setup.spec.js runs the same setup from three states (alternative\nselected with the sequence consumed, delays and CORS off; endpoints\ndisabled with Proxy All on; repeated without restore). It checks the\nreal fetches from the nginx page, and the traffic read page by page\nfrom the Monitor after a since=latest cursor, with no gap. It also\ncovers:\n- a select:false variant that leaves response, selection and sequence\n  cursor unchanged;\n- a 409 REVISION_CONFLICT between two clients;\n- the cleared gap after a Monitor clear;\n- setup errors that stop before mutating.\n\nThe stream-reload restore now refuses an empty seed instead of emptying\nthe workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: link PR #9 in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: check every setup operation in the contract and the served response (T3 review)\n\nREQUIRED_OPERATIONS omitted operations the setup uses (GET /mocks, GET\nand PUT /mocks/{id}, the sequence state and the variant DELETE), so a\ncontract missing one of them was accepted and the setup began mutating.\nThe list now covers every operation the helper and its checks call. A\nstub serving the real /info and the real spec without PUT /mocks/{id}\nproves connect stops with CONTRACT_UNVERIFIABLE after the two reads.\n\nThe inactive preparation check now compares the response actually served\nby GET /agent-test/orders before and after the preparation, while the\ndraft still exists: deleting it reloads the runtime and would hide a\nserving regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8cc6bc337fa03f8de46c32df14f4036004119617","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/trees/8cc6bc337fa03f8de46c32df14f4036004119617"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/commits/dd8a6dbfc8ac943bfd9722ceda48f88ce8f1dbbe","verification":{"payload":"tree 8cc6bc337fa03f8de46c32df14f4036004119617\nparent 0be78c4afda6b8d90fd5ccbe6c1d0e6b6058623b\nauthor tosdan <3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790810551 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790810551 +0200\n\ntest: cover the repeatable agent setup through API, browser and Monitor (T3) (#9)\n\n* test: cover the repeatable agent setup through API, browser and Monitor (T3)\n\nAdd mockxy-setup, a standalone instance with the admin API whose CORS\nstarts disabled, and an external setup helper (tests/agent-setup.js). It\nchecks the served contract and the workspace, declares CORS and delays\nthrough PATCH /config, prepares contents with the revision it read, then\nactivates and resets, failing with a diagnostic code instead of\nretrying.\n\nagent-setup.spec.js runs the same setup from three states (alternative\nselected with the sequence consumed, delays and CORS off; endpoints\ndisabled with Proxy All on; repeated without restore). It checks the\nreal fetches from the nginx page, and the traffic read page by page\nfrom the Monitor after a since=latest cursor, with no gap. It also\ncovers:\n- a select:false variant that leaves response, selection and sequence\n  cursor unchanged;\n- a 409 REVISION_CONFLICT between two clients;\n- the cleared gap after a Monitor clear;\n- setup errors that stop before mutating.\n\nThe stream-reload restore now refuses an empty seed instead of emptying\nthe workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: link PR #9 in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: check every setup operation in the contract and the served response (T3 review)\n\nREQUIRED_OPERATIONS omitted operations the setup uses (GET /mocks, GET\nand PUT /mocks/{id}, the sequence state and the variant DELETE), so a\ncontract missing one of them was accepted and the setup began mutating.\nThe list now covers every operation the helper and its checks call. A\nstub serving the real /info and the real spec without PUT /mocks/{id}\nproves connect stops with CONTRACT_UNVERIFIABLE after the two reads.\n\nThe inactive preparation check now compares the response actually served\nby GET /agent-test/orders before and after the preparation, while the\ndraft still exists: deleting it reloads the runtime and would hide a\nserving regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvZm3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVKMQAHZHNWN0gzsOwiIZGgxh127p\nBpQOzfvtTvGHvQZSUOCg56YtqDcuPia0eHNzhvVZZMDMdfRw865Y/+O/C6QkNawy\nzFmV43i7nZwkyymMj9JtTAZDhLgS2UPdMqbrY7YT0Ai5OJeFR8n4eZMULSZW8xzP\nQRpADRvWHJI4ZXgkDR231s08c0/jh/A/D+8CXO+WLKDnKQmrrdDOIOWa4Xl1p2OR\nCKfZBXy1