"login":"tosdan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY2OTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/117e699ff94673b4b653605efbd3c0a691982345/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:49:44Z","email":"3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"tosdan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:49:44Z","email":"3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"tosdan"},"message":"docs: mark T2 completed in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ce8c6488f38602093e1af0f5dad07472c08ee95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/trees/7ce8c6488f38602093e1af0f5dad07472c08ee95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/commits/117e699ff94673b4b653605efbd3c0a691982345","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3496697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan","id":3496697,"login":"tosdan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY2OTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commit/117e699ff94673b4b653605efbd3c0a691982345","node_id":"C_kwDOTUX0U9oAKDExN2U2OTlmZjk0NjczYjRiNjUzNjA1ZWZiZDNjMGE2OTE5ODIzNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commit/8dcec08ef115eb8194b621e28fe869b813251d96","sha":"8dcec08ef115eb8194b621e28fe869b813251d96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/8dcec08ef115eb8194b621e28fe869b813251d96"}],"sha":"117e699ff94673b4b653605efbd3c0a691982345","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/117e699ff94673b4b653605efbd3c0a691982345"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3496697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tosdan","id":3496697,"login":"tosdan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY2OTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tosdan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/commits/8dcec08ef115eb8194b621e28fe869b813251d96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:48:39Z","email":"3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"tosdan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:48:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: cover stream continuity and diagnostics across reloads (T2) (#8)\n\n* test: cover stream continuity and diagnostics across reloads (T2)\n\nAdd mockxy-stream, a development-image instance with the watcher and the\nadmin API, whose seed is copied to tmpfs and edited through\ndocker compose exec. The healthcheck also waits for the watcher.\n\nstream-reload.spec.js opens SSE and WebSocket connections from the\nbrowser and checks that description changes, inactive variants and\nunrelated endpoints (via API and via the watcher) keep them open with no\nhidden EventSource reconnection; that a changed SSE or WS script closes\nonly its own connection; that an unreadable new SSE definition keeps the\nprevious stream served and reported as retained; and that a broken\nhandler keeps serving until the fix clears the error and advances the\ndiagnostics revision. Every test restores the seed and waits for a\nstable runtime, even after a failure.\n\nThe client page gains named EventSource helpers that record opens and\nerrors, and WebSocket close tracking.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: link PR #8 in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: fix WS helper cleanup and drop racy attempt cause check (T2 review)\n\nThe WebSocket callbacks read the named registry, which wsCloseAll empties\nbefore the asynchronous close event arrives: the handler threw a\nTypeError in the page, or could mark a new connection with the same name\nas closed. Callbacks now capture their own entry, and wsCloseAll returns\na promise that resolves once the sockets are closed. Each stream-reload\ntest now fails on any page error, checked after cleanup.\n\n/runtime/status keeps only the last attempt, so the watcher echo can\nreplace the one caused by the admin mutations: the test no longer\nrequires the \"admin\" cause, only the attempt advancing, the served\ncontent and stream continuity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab53264f7cefb3e5113381b50579739b85436ddc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/trees/ab53264f7cefb3e5113381b50579739b85436ddc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tosdan/mockxy-acceptance-tests/git/commits/8dcec08ef115eb8194b621e28fe869b813251d96","verification":{"payload":"tree ab53264f7cefb3e5113381b50579739b85436ddc\nparent 1b0a43492f8e2139550bd4df32179cc49d1c2587\nauthor tosdan <3496697+tosdan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790794119 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790794119 +0200\n\ntest: cover stream continuity and diagnostics across reloads (T2) (#8)\n\n* test: cover stream continuity and diagnostics across reloads (T2)\n\nAdd mockxy-stream, a development-image instance with the watcher and the\nadmin API, whose seed is copied to tmpfs and edited through\ndocker compose exec. The healthcheck also waits for the watcher.\n\nstream-reload.spec.js opens SSE and WebSocket connections from the\nbrowser and checks that description changes, inactive variants and\nunrelated endpoints (via API and via the watcher) keep them open with no\nhidden EventSource reconnection; that a changed SSE or WS script closes\nonly its own connection; that an unreadable new SSE definition keeps the\nprevious stream served and reported as retained; and that a broken\nhandler keeps serving until the fix clears the error and advances the\ndiagnostics revision. Every test restores the seed and waits for a\nstable runtime, even after a failure.\n\nThe client page gains named EventSource helpers that record opens and\nerrors, and WebSocket close tracking.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: link PR #8 in the acceptance checklist\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: fix WS helper cleanup and drop racy attempt cause check (T2 review)\n\nThe WebSocket callbacks read the named registry, which wsCloseAll empties\nbefore the asynchronous close event arrives: the handler threw a\nTypeError in the page, or could mark a new connection with the same name\nas closed. Callbacks now capture their own entry, and wsCloseAll returns\na promise that resolves once the sockets are closed. Each stream-reload\ntest now fails on any page error, checked after cleanup.\n\n/runtime/status keeps only the last attempt, so the watcher echo can\nreplace the one caused by the admin mutations: the test no longer\nrequires the \"admin\" cause, only the attempt advancing, the served\ncontent and stream continuity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVmHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz/cQAJQgogZOT/OxVQ7CQRRYdlOn\n1UE7MUhuGPm2xcaslXqjJTjFfpcfa2GIvePSnN/Lm0WccQ+8BDKNVpNp5LehDZ24\nefnRHKHLN6JfpLi+GHVSeq+tKd5rhq72VnRXeqJiTZ9zeVebegGoWsCqfqMN8EY0\njbSla+Fel4WlqVTJyvYSWSQNJ2/onT3V2s/0j8kRTp9bg12x7e5HOz4DGIjBz6Zr\nM8261zeCF56oy8ZowOkb8gPCZ8scW+iIU9uLiHd29wrun1bRjtgpHd6pLkKjqly2\nQ68VY09dt4i/k/7YFCJjUEYn6LBeIt9QXvIkbiyR3keLwMamr2mQHQRQu+YqBSai\n2EjjrguozQknJq4iLvdFcPSdjs+7re5afPBvEc1/mk72E9GwC+Nl8/M6Lje6Fe1r\ntER7iyvDHFoxOb8HyA1SR3YshRqf2us+lDfNmdbuiK0N9iDqSJa2CbEyo3c0BAUe\n2KrgIgP8+ZNWk10bDd3jU3PqOVUP/51I2ovLhfaVdsxK8vpaytXzV0GXqfSo8Lu8\njzFiXuQ7LLxhQJwCni2Wy2bmYCeVhc3PMZw4QoMJFI8ZLADCC+DiQdG4uQjIcbDP\nBtquxX8NKuf0CGm5JTZGdm+XJzpSW9IMS1CRK+R2dvYCK9xDVVqnvZ14SZHzUjHk\naY2Z7/CS5thzRf6BtWxT\n=+1sh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:48:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198644