9Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"alexspeller","providerType":"User"},"email":"1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Speller"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:42:04.539Z","repositoryId":1296720835,"sha":"929445946dae41b4c1ec2e4ae98d814840fa856f"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:42:04.539Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1217?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller","id":1217,"login":"alexspeller","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/b41125929ab94dd8f2b2caba6accc7773507178d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:08:59Z","email":"1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Speller"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:08:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Test Firefox translation on long, live pages and React 19 (#6)\n\nThe real-Firefox harness drove one small React 18 page, updated only after\ntranslation had settled. It now runs three pages on React 18 and 19:\n\n- small page: each update is made while the nodes it touches are still the\n  ones Firefox''s merge left detached, and a precondition checks that they\n  are. Unmounting conditional text now comes first; before, a count update\n  re-attached it, so the removeChild the shim exists to repair was never\n  exercised against real Firefox.\n- long page: 150 sections, which Firefox translates lazily near the\n  viewport, updated between scrolls (counts, conditional text, an element\n  mounted before detached text, keyed rows), then read through a screen at\n  a time until every paragraph is translated and current.\n- racing: React re-renders every 40-310 ms while Firefox translates, with a\n  check that Firefox''s merges did detach React''s nodes mid-churn.\n\nEvery value React changes is a number, so a stale value shows whatever the\ntranslation. Updates wait until the DOM has been quiet, because Firefox\napplies a translation in flight on top of a text change made meanwhile (it\ncancels only on childList changes); the README now documents that race.\nAn independent review''s mutants (native removeChild; element groups never\nrestored), 0.4.1 and a no-op shim all fail it; the real build passes.\n\nReact 19 lives in scripts/react-19 with its own lockfile, installed by a\npretest:firefox hook, since react-dom 19 cannot share the root''s React 18.\nIt is bundled with esbuild, now an explicit dev dependency.","tree":{"sha":"526a7e9e21b7ba04a6892b018e67b58ab668f86e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/git/trees/526a7e9e21b7ba04a6892b018e67b58ab668f86e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/git/commits/b41125929ab94dd8f2b2caba6accc7773507178d","verification":{"payload":"tree 526a7e9e21b7ba04a6892b018e67b58ab668f86e\nparent 9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de\nauthor Alex Speller <1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com> 1790431739 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790431739 +0000\n\nTest Firefox translation on long, live pages and React 19 (#6)\n\nThe real-Firefox harness drove one small React 18 page, updated only after\ntranslation had settled. It now runs three pages on React 18 and 19:\n\n- small page: each update is made while the nodes it touches are still the\n  ones Firefox''s merge left detached, and a precondition checks that they\n  are. Unmounting conditional text now comes first; before, a count update\n  re-attached it, so the removeChild the shim exists to repair was never\n  exercised against real Firefox.\n- long page: 150 sections, which Firefox translates lazily near the\n  viewport, updated between scrolls (counts, conditional text, an element\n  mounted before detached text, keyed rows), then read through a screen at\n  a time until every paragraph is translated and current.\n- racing: React re-renders every 40-310 ms while Firefox translates, with a\n  check that Firefox''s merges did detach React''s nodes mid-churn.\n\nEvery value React changes is a number, so a stale value shows whatever the\ntranslation. Updates wait until the DOM has been quiet, because Firefox\napplies a translation in flight on top of a text change made meanwhile (it\ncancels only on childList changes); the README now documents that race.\nAn independent review''s mutants (native removeChild; element groups never\nrestored), 0.4.1 and a no-op shim all fail it; the real build passes.\n\nReact 19 lives in scripts/react-19 with its own lockfile, installed by a\npretest:firefox hook, since react-dom 19 cannot share the root''s React 18.\nIt is bundled with esbuild, now an explicit dev dependency.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt9H7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA76wQAD9y03LePVIY/gvMqrg4IQ7w\nMnDf8dsyzsMe4g1cPLTFHLx2zlTCvB54L+ndwkCz+tfmiArWVkydvW/2s6VC16EH\napG85inylK3O/nKU5UOyxwHrrD9fsl58G+mxWmOYrLcjvoUYjml9LYXbTMjhQgY9\nbQDBMY3X4GEa39PlTm3e85Irdn3v2OLMxHic1VcLjlY4yzzuZ/+t6ViJPEVu0LWB\nsY+dZAUIbeW6JoQ35MsIomgP6wbeVCn4z5CZuzCW3rj5xuoe+7sLVlx3EKSJBaZ8\nuCHYasyOatZ/9zArzFyyWoXxElUrPR9E7R304fZ+PUBpPgiJ8VoBECeoM07dsZVp\nBhJBgvJaXWuj8rXUkpIT3RhWBtGPDblmpOTdeZIZDE8kimyyG8V0DX3vOEOhmRP1\nAN38NRDg/gkdGXEaND0ys0btnHUdnGcAzsKRJYJj1uMmAbGhN9R+IvgtA2k5EISN\nsz7VdEjfziSnez9dYmX/oDc9/vnay20WgihWzkzl2e7z+/RznciRSJfal1pznDrs\np4r+sIMQIz2gJwKtI8dHufJ8goN1P3QPzAB0ya1D+7G/0zpnaorOOEF4vkUuY3QO\nMmi6W5ayNx7ynJ8BTEITrSuyDzWMtWQPCvE8EJzhxfM+s96ZJbwudJFyVUemCiH4\ngIGpF07ETh/cMBR6V4RF\n=U3JB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T14:09:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commit/b41125929ab94dd8f2b2caba6accc7773507178d","node_id":"C_kwDOTUpjw9oAKGI0MTEyNTkyOWFiOTRkZDhmMmIyY2FiYTZhY2NjNzc3MzUwNzE3OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commit/9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de","sha":"9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de"}],"sha":"b41125929ab94dd8f2b2caba6accc7773507178d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/b41125929ab94dd8f2b2caba6accc7773507178d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1217?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller","id":1217,"login":"alexspeller","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T19:10:02Z","email":"1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Speller"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T19:10:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Support Firefox''s full-page translation (#5)\n\nFirefox''s translator (merge() in translations-document.sys.mjs) applies a\ntranslation by detaching every child of a block and appending the result\nback, reusing Text nodes by position. Its engine sees adjacent Text nodes\nas one run, so the first node of a run carries the whole translation and\nthe rest are never re-attached: React''s interpolations froze, and\nunmounting or inserting before them threw NotFoundError. Reproduced\nagainst real Firefox 153/156 with a React 18 page.\n\nArming: Firefox sets <html lang> as it starts. The <html> instance (not\nElement.prototype) gets wrappers for every Element API that writes\nattributes and for the lang setter; the page''s own writes go through\nthem and a translator''s never do, so apps syncing <html lang> (#1) stay\ndormant. Chrome''s own lang rewrite is recognised as Chrome''s once its\ntranslated-ltr/rtl class has been seen. Firefox''s data-moz-translations-id\ntags are a second signal, seen as they appear or found in place when an\neager observer starts late.\n\nRecognition, only once Firefox''s signal has been seen: a parent emptied\nfirst-to-last and refilled by appends reusing a removed Text node, every\nreused node overwritten, and none of the nodes moved by the page through\nthe patched methods. A lossy merge gets a whole-parent group - original\nchildren in order with their pre-translation text - restored before any\nrenderer operation on a member; Firefox then re-translates the restored\nnodes one by one, in place.\n\nAlso: restores discard their own mutation records; duplicate copies of\nthe package chain and unwind each other''s <html> wrappers; uninstall is\nfault-contained; the translated-* class is matched as exact tokens.\n\nTests: jsdom specs for every failure mode and review finding, a Firefox\nmode in the simulator (translateLikeFirefox / mergeLikeFirefox), real\nChrome checks for isolated-world lang writes, and npm run test:firefox,\nwhich drives Firefox''s own translator over Marionette in CI and\nprepublishOnly. Four rounds of independent review.\n\nBumps to 0.5.0.","tree":{"sha":"d47f7f3ca00586ec91826a64ef2a2265b388e64d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/git/trees/d47f7f3ca00586ec91826a64ef2a2265b388e64d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/git/commits/9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de","verification":{"payload":"tree d47f7f3ca00586ec91826a64ef2a2265b388e64d\nparent 99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43\nauthor Alex Speller <1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com> 1790363402 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790363402 +0000\n\nSupport Firefox''s full-page translation (#5)\n\nFirefox''s translator (merge() in translations-document.sys.mjs) applies a\ntranslation by detaching every child of a block and appending the result\nback, reusing Text nodes by position. Its engine sees adjacent Text nodes\nas one run, so the first node of a run carries the whole translation and\nthe rest are never re-attached: React''s interpolations froze, and\nunmounting or inserting before them threw NotFoundError. Reproduced\nagainst real Firefox 153/156 with a React 18 page.\n\nArming: Firefox sets <html lang> as it starts. The <html> instance (not\nElement.prototype) gets wrappers for every Element API that writes\nattributes and for the lang setter; the page''s own writes go through\nthem and a translator''s never do, so apps syncing <html lang> (#1) stay\ndormant. Chrome''s own lang rewrite is recognised as Chrome''s once its\ntranslated-ltr/rtl class has been seen. Firefox''s data-moz-translations-id\ntags are a second signal, seen as they appear or found in place when an\neager observer starts late.\n\nRecognition, only once Firefox''s signal has been seen: a parent emptied\nfirst-to-last and refilled by appends reusing a removed Text node, every\nreused node overwritten, and none of the nodes moved by the page through\nthe patched methods. A lossy merge gets a whole-parent group - original\nchildren in order with their pre-translation text - restored before any\nrenderer operation on a member; Firefox then re-translates the restored\nnodes one by one, in place.\n\nAlso: restores discard their own mutation records; duplicate copies of\nthe package chain and unwind each other''s <html> wrappers; uninstall is\nfault-contained; the translated-* class is matched as exact tokens.\n\nTests: jsdom specs for every failure mode and review finding, a Firefox\nmode in the simulator (translateLikeFirefox / mergeLikeFirefox), real\nChrome checks for isolated-world lang writes, and npm run test:firefox,\nwhich drives Firefox''s own translator over Marionette in CI and\nprepublishOnly. Four rounds of independent review.\n\nBumps to 0.5.0.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtscKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZDYQAKAZM6F2MVyVx7HarPYCkOcu\nSi56Yz+SWl37/ijqDKtJLbPPlDXQGyXZHaQzFM8bbgNM7NUl/93BOz6jIwX6PAbL\nNd9NVAO2tf46bS45XiGCwiV3MciUlTvs7w5c54wX3XWHtMKKUAiNC+N7TDJeiIB4\nC1YKyOwJcuK5ZN6BUjhb+ek1ZXRAoMyeLh9zQoAcKJGu+7tIdEyNPuJDf9FvtYZO\nyuMxq4v76/LkCA/HeCGKibytZTb3j/Y9WoaAZfi0vQTLqmL0p78+sY2RfA95rnly\n58iLcnVBRN3NP+4bhcL533M/XCZACxA/cdhA94EQeaDw1S/AkUUnzG+vDP0rAOGY\nyaWS6+7DPyxt/WJxPk4oxJBrxzRBsngw+WDIIL5Ukrg66b+aq0JQFsEOcTZbXy7w\noDJpKHbITopGntvTg6rcw1HiSrX1vGSWKpRdI4P1pIbIVT995+0/SwoEjByDwx3w\nL1vwtXTkJ0Cmca9g1ntzSZ2SjwGjVXbRfH4sgKZ4RW7YKodSibETOtOox/9WEwpt\nq6cY1/9DrHsrAOXzpY6w/Pn5Gbc8shNQ8t5nOOr/7rFf8zk9g5hZzSTMYCd+yHWd\nGiUSOCPj6mny1mMSIpTnA/k09qk1PMI6yeTsoHZm7uCKOgR9Uiw2+BKnsQoEYT2E\nP5RK61OkOhmb3tSPfkTx\n=ejUU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T19:10:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commit/9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de","node_id":"C_kwDOTUpjw9oAKDlkNWQ5Y2Q3N2VjZDBhY2I5M2Q3ZDM0NTJmMDEyZTI5M2I3MDQ4ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commit/99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43","sha":"99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43"}],"sha":"9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/9d5d9cd77ecd0acb93d7d3452f012e293b7048de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1217?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller","id":1217,"login":"alexspeller","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:24:22Z","email":"1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Speller"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:24:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop treating <html lang> writes as a translation signal (#4)\n\nThe lazy sentinel armed the document-wide observer on any mutation of\n<html lang>. Apps write that attribute themselves - i18n libraries sync\nit when language detection resolves and on every switch (WCAG 3.1.1) -\nso every such app ran the full observer for the whole session, and the\nlazy default was unavailable to it.\n\nThe sentinel now watches only the translated-* class. lang bought no\ncoverage: Google''s translate script adds the class first, in the same\ncall, and only rewrites a lang the page already has; Edge and the\nGoogle Translate extension never touch it; Firefox flips it, but its\ndetach-and-re-append merge is not a shape the observer recognises, so\narming early changed nothing there.\n\nAlso makes browser-test wait for Chrome to exit before removing its temp\nprofile: the immediate rmSync raced Chrome''s helper processes (ENOTEMPTY)\nafter every check had passed.\n\nFixes #1","tree":{"sha":"fd1590c7a416698d75976cbd18c8bf9e4b3cd358","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/git/trees/fd1590c7a416698d75976cbd18c8bf9e4b3cd358"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/git/commits/99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43","verification":{"payload":"tree fd1590c7a416698d75976cbd18c8bf9e4b3cd358\nparent cff5986ee3c7b5f2c8ef557097b30b619fb56299\nauthor Alex Speller <1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com> 1790357062 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790357062 +0000\n\nStop treating <html lang> writes as a translation signal (#4)\n\nThe lazy sentinel armed the document-wide observer on any mutation of\n<html lang>. Apps write that attribute themselves - i18n libraries sync\nit when language detection resolves and on every switch (WCAG 3.1.1) -\nso every such app ran the full observer for the whole session, and the\nlazy default was unavailable to it.\n\nThe sentinel now watches only the translated-* class. lang bought no\ncoverage: Google''s translate script adds the class first, in the same\ncall, and only rewrites a lang the page already has; Edge and the\nGoogle Translate extension never touch it; Firefox flips it, but its\ndetach-and-re-append merge is not a shape the observer recognises, so\narming early changed nothing there.\n\nAlso makes browser-test wait for Chrome to exit before removing its temp\nprofile: the immediate rmSync raced Chrome''s helper processes (ENOTEMPTY)\nafter every check had passed.\n\nFixes #1","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtq5GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAs8QAEMDG+dfDP2wb1ozdUMKtFR4\nJDuYNYykoFw38vAOGWyawCZ4PNDjzqDQyKyNfTw2+uogfhG09t1viHCmq+XhIkC/\nQboUGvpqrdK2OrbJ8Jcoyx7S8nmx3YGVn/ExsI3/amAfOFPQvBDUkz3U+Kqg0tLt\nusObHtX2PDQYorCvQEQwSdrD4gdsrvwVwIg2XSZG0XVRWPBbqE4Dh74qVIZb5w/V\nBe/Ble57o/cl/wbAaWkvmmp5r3s3DwQhQVN2hgc+037Cxw3ihVPnsIzvmflUIgOX\naXjVfH53qZ2Fn7+Ic+DkiNpKPIGr/EtaHd8jEWcSbheg7hmBk9wrWjGvZbtf15+Y\nWVm5bb42jzqeot4ck+gGsqOXFwoKFnxdS8BwaLmjYVGcqGWkHX60fLkhYU2MYSGh\ng08vpJn4u/hqYhyIetRDc18g04XCgtIMktYjrexVraucD7a+EsZWZDdLuALODx9f\nfbrcrWRboSMHz8OF887P/BQ8iZIH4gB9fB6ssAMGljLwqOugT/CdT0gdfvwT7MTB\nbrnKjACYJBFb1nLMfOtcGbtTHxgHPH5RC/HZEnK6T4lBz46YGeQgid41IqWqca07\nllQWHhHICFDNfGnCL2/JjY9LZJuvd7Eimr4aTsBqFyqg+c2wehUwbj6RsJ7wWUD+\nnsaQDdILaOlOOPYFvxcW\n=DoGT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T17:24:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commit/99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43","node_id":"C_kwDOTUpjw9oAKDk5YWRkY2Q0ZWJlZDI5YThlNzdjOGQ4MTlmZGYxOGE0OWVjZDdkNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commit/cff5986ee3c7b5f2c8ef557097b30b619fb56299","sha":"cff5986ee3c7b5f2c8ef557097b30b619fb56299","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/cff5986ee3c7b5f2c8ef557097b30b619fb56299"}],"sha":"99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/99addcd4ebed29a8e77c8d819fdf18a49ecd7d43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1217?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexspeller","id":1217,"login":"alexspeller","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexspeller","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/commits/cff5986ee3c7b5f2c8ef557097b30b619fb56299/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T12:12:53Z","email":"1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Speller"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T12:12:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Arm on translator markup the isolated world can actually raise (#3)\n\nBrowser translators run in the engine''s own isolated world: they share the\nDOM but hold a separate copy of Node.prototype, so they never call this\npackage''s patched methods. Arming on a signature <font> seen by patched\ninsertBefore/appendChild could therefore only ever fire for a same-realm\ntranslator like the bundled simulator — which is exactly what the tests\nused, so the gap stayed green in CI while React kept crashing on Edge.\n\nDetection now hangs a 1ms CSS animation off the translator''s signature\n<font> and arms on animationstart, which fires whichever world inserted\nit (+1.1% on a churn benchmark, against +7.2% for the childList observer\nthis replaces the need for). It installs as a constructable stylesheet so\na style-src CSP cannot disable it. Anything still unrecognised is caught\non the way to NotFoundError, where a document sweep distinguishes a\ntranslated page from a genuine renderer bug; that also covers a restore\nthat lands the reference node under a different parent, which previously\nfell through to the native call and threw.","tree":{"sha":"20e6d92d8e45053ecf5b8a6b5fea058d237b623d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/git/trees/20e6d92d8e45053ecf5b8a6b5fea058d237b623d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexspeller/translation-resilience/git/commits/cff5986ee3c7b5f2c8ef557097b30b619fb56299","verification":{"payload":"tree 20e6d92d8e45053ecf5b8a6b5fea058d237b623d\nparent 622276073e6fa8f37655dc0faa42c3db8248cbe6\nauthor Alex Speller <1217+alexspeller@users.noreply.github.com> 1789560773 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789560773 +0000\n\nArm on translator markup the isolated world can actually raise (#3)\n\nBrowser translators run in the engine''s own isolated world: they share the\nDOM but hold a separate copy of Node.prototype, so they never call this\npackage''s patched methods. Arming on a signature <font> seen by patched\ninsertBefore/appendChild could therefore only ever fire for a same-realm\ntranslator like the bundled simulator — which is exactly what the tests\nused, so the gap stayed green in CI while React kept crashing on Edge.\n\nDetection now hangs a 1ms CSS animation off the translator''s signature\n<font> and arms on animationstart, which fires whichever world inserted\nit (+1.1% on a churn benchmark, against +7.2% for the childList observer\nthis replaces the need for). It installs as a constructable stylesheet so\na style-src CSP cannot disable it. Anything still unrecognised is caught\non the way to NotFoundError, where a document sweep distinguishes a\ntranslated page from a genuine renderer bug; that also covers a restore\nthat lands the reference node under a different parent, which previously\nfell through to the native call and threw.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqofFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2k0QAKezb7WSE4ZAsJCKSYq9Eynv\n6q2l+k2CGqo6C8wF/8iDIN4wezuDV6M/NQfr9doMjcc1m4EPXp1zkNws0rFx6UtW\nmVZs6cKmvIUQ0Iv5hQPikD10okDfcEfcNXz6vM+71B9edSc0MvW+0r4AnDkRXnPz\nrfDFWH1whdc4FmE78fMItmKuvHdfFdxkhVnaER1oc6tyMTk0dDzGXVEYqPR5bJwm\noT/1SRbX7EmS/XGlGlcW4lfB3sREPLy/VG6jHpiRPrBBXn02gek1xVDcuoQv+4dq\nI/EQx1sygIW/HYge6/7PwIBBYNUZDCO5k/D4suBRJTMHzQwjyXgqiPJ9VISBHR2K\nd7Qs0o+xPUpfhkacghCNo9WxbDhSDcVkSW+TRyFBx/v59WXyVkHvxzpIBZNrjG0m\nNxXHXV3O1qG8wlfYmR8IJnSupXiaAUwosAZIpu7ls/XuqLbL/ufVoTgvDHIzPqQc\n3RPeCtBrrjHfCTPLgEGF/X7F3m4SlKWyRhq+ipbUxoHQ3th65ureRqnOM1Z0lFyu\nBobwN23GWZJmYtpUIT/twbdW8iryFfb+qwAEx03MRsjSceYY